# HTTP Server in C

A minimal HTTP server written in **C** using TCP sockets.

## Features

* TCP socket-based HTTP server
* `GET` — read files and list directories
* `POST` — create files
* `PUT` — create or update files
* `DELETE` — delete files
* Automatic `Content-Type` detection
* HTML directory listing
* Web interface using JavaScript `fetch()`

## Requirements

* Linux
* GCC
* cURL

Install the dependencies on Ubuntu/Debian:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install build-essential curl
```

## Build

```bash
gcc -Wall -Wextra -g main.c -o main
```

## Run

```bash
./main
```

The server listens on port `8000`.

Open your browser:

```text
http://localhost:8000/
```

## Testing

### GET

```bash
curl -i http://localhost:8000/
curl -i http://localhost:8000/main.c
```

### POST

```bash
curl -i -X POST http://localhost:8000/test.txt -d "Hello HTTP"
```

### PUT

```bash
curl -i -X PUT http://localhost:8000/test.txt -d "Updated content"
```

### DELETE

```bash
curl -i -X DELETE http://localhost:8000/test.txt
```

## Architecture

```text
Browser / cURL
      |
      | HTTP
      v
+----------------+
|  HTTP Server   |
|      in C      |
+-------+--------+
        |
        v
   File System
```

The **browser or cURL** acts as the HTTP client, while the **C program** acts as the HTTP server.

## Project Structure

```text
.
├── main.c
├── ds.h
└── README.md
```

## Educational Goal

This project is designed to understand:

* TCP sockets
* HTTP requests and responses
* HTTP methods
* File I/O
* MIME types
* Client-server communication
* JavaScript `fetch()`
